# Build context for the scraper-service image.
#
# Every entry here is either (a) large, (b) a build output that would be
# COPYed into the image stale, or (c) secret material that must never reach a
# layer. The Docker build only needs: src/, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock,
# scrape_media.py, and the Dockerfile itself.

# Build outputs — the image compiles its own. Note the repo .gitignore uses
# `**/target/**`, which .dockerignore patterns do NOT inherit, so target/ is
# listed explicitly. Sending the host's 1GB target/ would be pure waste.
target/
**/target/

# Dependencies and VCS metadata
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
**/.git/

# Secrets and environment — these must never be baked into a layer, where they
# persist in the image history even if a later RUN deletes them.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/secrets/

# Logs and caches
*.log
**/*.log
.cache/
**/.cache/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Deploy + CI plumbing that has no business in a runtime image
deploy/
infra/
scripts/
ecosystem.config.cjs
check_image_cache_db.sh
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Tests are not run in the image; excluding them keeps the context small and
# keeps test-only dev-dependencies (sea-orm "mock") out of the build.
tests/
**/tests/
**/*.test.rs

# Python helpers that are NOT the Playwright fallback this service shells out
# to. scrape_media.py is deliberately NOT excluded — Dockerfile copies it into
# the runtime layer, because downloader/shared.rs resolves it next to the
# running binary.
stalk_tiktok.py
**/stalk_tiktok.py
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Docs and markdown scratch/notes — not runtime input.
docs/
**/docs/
**/*.md
!README.md

# infra/ and tooling
tools/
**/tools/
**/node_modules/**/.bin/
moon.yml
.moon/